---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/Mark.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Ekphrasis — a macOS image-to-sound instrument"
  description="Ekphrasis is a macOS VST3/AU/Standalone instrument that reads an image as a spectrogram — brightness becomes amplitude, height becomes frequency — and resynthesizes it into sound."
>
  <h1 class="flex items-center gap-4"><Mark name="ekphrasis" size={72} />Ekphrasis</h1>
  <p>
    An instrument that reads a picture as a spectrogram and plays it back as
    sound.
  </p>

  <h2>How it reads an image</h2>
  <p>
    A spectrogram is a picture of a sound: time runs left to right, frequency
    runs bottom to top, and brightness is how much energy is there. Ekphrasis
    takes any image and reads it as though it were one — a pixel's
    <strong>vertical position</strong> sets a partial's frequency, its
    <strong>brightness</strong> sets that partial's amplitude — then
    resynthesizes the result. The picture becomes something you can play.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>VST3, AU, and a standalone app</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <p>macOS 11.0 or later.</p>

  <p>
    Ekphrasis ships as a signed, notarized installer for the AU, the VST3 and
    a standalone app.
  </p>
  <p><Button href="/ekphrasis/download">Download Ekphrasis</Button></p>
</Base>
